  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data explored** (`kibana_sample_data_logs`): 14,074 requests from about 1,000 client IPs, spanning 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03. The main fields are `response` (200 for 12,832 requests, 404 for 801, 503 for 441), `bytes`, `clientip`, `geo.dest` (173 countries), `extension`, `url`, and `agent`. The only 5xx code present is 503.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-b7cc417c Web logs overview\"** (`eff-b7cc417c-web-logs-overview-7352165b21a6`)\n- Total requests (count)\n- Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n- Total bytes served (sum of `bytes`)\n- Requests over time (area chart, date histogram)\n- Responses by status code (pie, top 10 `response.keyword`)\n- 5xx responses (ES|QL metric)\n\nThe time range is set to 2026-09-01 through 2027-01-01 so it covers the sample data. Today is 2026-10-11, and the data runs to December.\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-b7cc417c 5xx spike\"** (id `240ac844-8ce4-48c6-bdbc-dcdfa0c0d452`)\n- Type `.es-query`, consumer `stackAlerts`, running every 1m.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` over the last 5 minutes, and fires when the count is above 10.\n- Status is `ok` and enabled is `true`. Alerting health is `ok`.\n- The query returns 441 hits, the same as the response breakdown.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- The rule has no connector attached, so it will track state but send no notifications. Say if you want one, for example a server-log or Slack connector.\n- The rule is tagged `EFF-b7cc417c`.\n- Because the sample data is dated in the future relative to today, the 5-minute window may often be empty. That is expected for a rule like this.",
